# Light typography — one break, true center, forever

When a Light sentence is shown in **Sky main** and on the **Light card** (including export/share), the line break / primary+accent split MUST be identical. Copy must never look glued to the right edge.

## Hard rules

- Use only `getAlbumTypoLines()` from `components/vora/mirror-album-typo.ts` for sentence splitting **and** visual lines (`primaryLines` / `accentLines`).
- Render via `AlbumTypoBlock` — each line in `.vora-album-typo-row` (full-width flex center) + `.vora-album-typo-line` (`nowrap`). Layout also lives in `album-typo-block.module.css` so Turbopack cannot resurrect a stale globals rule. Never free-wrap plain strings; never rely on CSS to invent breaks.
- **Safe inset:** Light card body uses symmetric `--vora-light-card-copy-inset` (≈2.5rem). Sky uses `--vora-sky-copy-inset` (≈2.15rem). Do not shrink horizontal padding to “fit more text.” Export keeps equal left/right padding too.
- **Center forever:** `.vora-album-typo-row` = `display:flex; justify-content:center`; `.vora-album-typo-line` = `width:max-content; max-width:none; nowrap`. **Never** `left:50%`, translate hacks, or `max-width:100%` on nowrap lines — when ink > box, `text-align:center` pins left and spills right (Sky looks right-skewed; card looks fine because type is smaller).
- **Optical tracking (Sky vs Card):** Sky type is much larger, so letter-spacing drift is obvious on main and quiet on card. Always apply `--vora-typo-hero-track-fix` / `--vora-typo-accent-track-fix` on album lines (`padding-inline-end` / `padding-inline-start`). Missing track-fix = “main looks right-shifted, card looks fine.”
- Sky headline measure should stay wide (`--vora-mirror-headline-width` on `.vora-sky-todays-light`); tame `--vora-typo-sky-*` so long lines usually fit the phone width.

## Editorial split (feel first)

- **Primary (Instrument)** = quieter setup.
- **Accent (Rosemartin)** = the landing you feel.
- Strong heads: `every`, `never`, `always`, `only`, `still`…
- Soft + relative: keep soft on **primary**; start accent at `who` / `what` / `which`.
  - Mobile card is the measure limit (accent type is larger + safe inset). Never invent a longer accent line that overflows the card.
  - Example: `I attract success through who I am becoming.`
    - primary: `I attract` / `success through`
    - accent: `who I am` / `becoming.`
  - Never one long setup line ending in `through` on Sky — reads right-skewed.
  - Never put `through who I am` on accent — overflows the card.
  - **LOCKED:** `LOCKED_ALBUM_TYPO` in `mirror-album-typo.ts` hard-codes this poster. `reclaimSoftBeforeRelative` catches algorithm leaks. Run `pnpm test:typo` after typography edits.
- Prefer a substantial punch word alone on the last accent line when it reads as the landing (`becoming`, `enough`, `myself`…).
- Never end a line on hanging `I` / `to` / `my` unless the next line is that intentional punch word (`who I am` → `becoming`).
- **Short fits = one line:** If a phrase fits the char budget (`LINE_BUDGET` / `ACCENT_LINE_BUDGET`), keep it on one line. Do not binary-split just because there are 4 words — `I can do it` is one breath.

## Why

Different breaks = a different sentence. Edge-hugging or right-drift kills quiet craft.
